$ An MPC with a scalar point as its independent term: GRID 1 T3 = u(1002). Scalar point 1002 is on a spring k = 10 to
$ the held scalar point 1001, with a unit SLOAD on it, so u(1002) = 1 / 10 = 0.1 and GRID 1 T3 = 0.1 (hand values).
$ A scalar-point term read at the wrong DOF ties GRID 1 T3 to the held point 1001 (0) instead.
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE = MPC WITH A SCALAR POINT AS INDEPENDENT TERM
SPC = 1
MPC = 1
LOAD = 1
DISPLACEMENT = ALL
BEGIN BULK
GRID,1,,0.,0.,0.,,12456
SPOINT,1001,1002
SPC1,1,0,1001
CELAS4,11,10.,1002,1001
MPC,1,1,3,1.,1002,0,-1.
SLOAD,1,1002,1.
ENDDATA
